// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 15-function-semantics
// facility: [T-Call] (each argument at its parameter's type, rule.fn.closure); [Closure-Call]; conf.closure-argument-type
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.type-mismatch (static)
//
// A closure's parameter types bind its calls as a named function's do: an
// `i32` is not an `i64` (D-0006: no implicit conversion). The argument's
// type had not been compared, so the call ran, converting.

import std;

fn main()
{
    auto twice = [](i64 v) : i64 { v * 2 };
    i32 x = 21;
    printf("%v\n", twice(x));
}
